<!--
    Swift register-specific retain/release entry points.

    Issue: an optimized arm64 Swift caller releases or retains an object
    through the runtime's `swift_release_x<N>` / `swift_retain_x<N>` entry
    points (`swift/Runtime/CustomRRABI.h`), which take the object in `x<N>`
    instead of `x0`. Under the C model no parameter lives there, so every such
    call printed with no argument: `swift_release_x20();`.

    Stage / sub-stage: P1 external-refinement, `SwiftRuntimePass`
    (`kuna-analysis/src/analyzers/swift/kuna_swiftruntime.rs`). No option: the
    entry points are the runtime's ABI, like the rest of the table.

    The fixture `swift_rr_regs_macho` (arm64 Mach-O, assembled from
    `swift_rr_regs_macho.s` against the iOS 16.5 libswiftCore) imports
    `swift_retain`, `swift_release_x20`, `swift_retain_x21`,
    `swift_bridgeObjectRetain_x22` and `swift_bridgeObjectRelease_x23`.
    `keep_first` releases its second argument through `x20`; `retain_second`
    retains its second argument through `x21` and stores the result, which the
    entry point returns in `x0`; `bridge_swap` retains a bridge object through
    `x22` and releases another through `x23`.
-->
